{"id": "77acc6d5-c8fd-47de-95d4-a5b8b2f5fd65", "role": "assistant", "block_type": "thinking", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "I'm recalling that this is a known AWS issue where Rekognition video APIs need the SNS topic configured with a specific resource policy granting Rekognition permission to publish, rather than relying solely on IAM role permissions.

The key gotcha is that AmazonRekognitionServiceRole's managed policy only grants sns:Publish permission to topics matching the naming pattern "AmazonRekognition*" - so a topic named something else like "video-done" would silently fail to receive notifications even though StartLabelDetection itself succeeds. I should verify this specific claim about the policy's resource restriction before concluding this is a denial scenario.

"}]}

